# 📅 Tuesday — Filtering, Sorting & Search

## 🎯 Goal

Make `GET /api/users` more useful without exposing the whole query object to MongoDB.

## 1️⃣ Filtering — Allowlist Only

Only approved parameters are read. Everything else is ignored.

```js
function buildFilter(queryParams) {
    const filter = {};
    if (queryParams.role) {
        filter.role = queryParams.role;   // only "role" is approved
    }
    return filter;
}
```

Why? Prevents NoSQL injection like `?role[$ne]=null` from reaching MongoDB.

## 2️⃣ Search — Case-Insensitive, Escaped

Searches `name` or `email` for the text (case-insensitive):

```js
filter.$or = [
    { name:  { $regex: safeTerm, $options: "i" } },
    { email: { $regex: safeTerm, $options: "i" } }
];
```

Before using the term, escape regex characters:

```js
function escapeRegex(text) {
    return text.replace(/[.*+?^${}()|[\]\\]/g, "\\$&");
}
```

This prevents ReDoS — a malicious regex freezing the database.

## 3️⃣ Sorting

`?sort=name` → ascending
`?sort=-createdAt` → descending (prefix `-`)

```js
function buildSort(queryParams) {
    if (!queryParams.sort) return { createdAt: -1 };
    const field = queryParams.sort;
    const desc = field.startsWith("-");
    const name = desc ? field.substring(1) : field;
    return { [name]: desc ? -1 : 1 };
}
```

## 4️⃣ Field Selection

`?fields=name,email` returns only those fields (plus `_id`).

```js
function buildFieldSelection(queryParams) {
    if (!queryParams.fields) return "-password -__v -refreshTokenHash";
    return queryParams.fields.split(",").join(" ");
}
```

## 5️⃣ All Combined

```
GET /api/users?role=user&search=example&sort=-createdAt&fields=name,email&page=1&limit=5
```

Pagination metadata reflects the **filtered** set, not the full collection.

