# 📅 Wednesday — Email Service (Nodemailer)

## 🎯 Goal

Send automated emails from the backend — welcome emails on registration, password-reset emails on request.

## 🔑 Access Tokens vs Setup

- Uses **Nodemailer** with **Gmail SMTP**
- Requires a **Gmail App Password** (not the regular password)
- Setup steps: enable 2FA → generate app password → paste into `.env`

```env
EMAIL_USER=your_email@gmail.com
EMAIL_PASS=your_app_password
EMAIL_FROM=your_email@gmail.com
```

## 🧩 Service Structure

```
services/email.service.js
    ├── sendWelcomeEmail(userEmail, userName)
    └── sendPasswordResetEmail(userEmail, resetToken)
```

## 📄 HTML Templates

HTML lives in separate files, not inside JavaScript strings:

```
templates/emails/
    ├── welcome.html
    └── reset-password.html
```

Placeholders use `{{variable}}` and are replaced at send time:

```html
<h1>Welcome, {{name}}! 🎉</h1>
```

A small `template.service.js` handles the replacement.

## 🛡️ Failure Handling

```js
try {
    await emailService.sendWelcomeEmail(user.email, user.name);
} catch (error) {
    console.error("⚠️ Welcome email failed:", error.message);
    // Do NOT crash — registration already succeeded
}
```

Emails fail silently without breaking the API.

---

# 📅 Thursday — Cloudinary Image Upload

## 🎯 Goal

Allow users to upload an avatar. Store the file in Cloudinary (not on the server disk).

```
Client selects image
     ↓
Multer reads multipart/form-data
     ↓
multer-storage-cloudinary uploads
     ↓
Cloudinary returns URL + publicId
     ↓
Server saves them in user document
```

## 🔧 Setup

- Packages: `multer`, `cloudinary`, `multer-storage-cloudinary`
- `config/cloudinary.js` — Cloudinary SDK config
- `middleware/upload.middleware.js` — Multer with Cloudinary storage

Allowed formats: `jpg, jpeg, png, gif, webp, jfif, heic`
Max size: **5 MB**
Auto-resize on upload

## 🗂️ Schema Addition

```js
avatar: {
    url: { type: String, default: null },
    publicId: { type: String, default: null }
}
```

The `publicId` is required to delete or replace the image later.

## 🔄 Replace Behavior

When a user uploads a new avatar:

```
Find user
   ↓
Has old publicId? → delete old image from Cloudinary
   ↓
Save new url + publicId
```

No orphaned files.

## 🗑️ Delete Behavior

```
DELETE /api/users/avatar
   ↓
Delete image from Cloudinary
   ↓
Set avatar.url and avatar.publicId to null
```

