# 📡 API Endpoints

## Public

| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|--------|----------|-------------|
| POST | `/api/users/register` | Register user (sends welcome email) |
| POST | `/api/users/login` | Login and receive JWT |
| POST | `/api/users/forgot-password` | Request password reset via email |
| POST | `/api/users/reset-password` | Reset password with token |

## Protected (`Authorization: Bearer <token>`)

| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|--------|----------|-------------|
| GET | `/api/users` | List users (paginated, filtered, sorted, searched) |
| GET | `/api/users/profile` | Current user's profile |
| POST | `/api/users/upload-avatar` | Upload or replace avatar |
| DELETE | `/api/users/avatar` | Delete avatar |

---

# ⚙️ Setup & Installation

### 1. Install

```bash
npm install express mongoose dotenv bcrypt jsonwebtoken nodemailer multer cloudinary multer-storage-cloudinary
```

### 2. Create `.env`

```env
PORT=3000
MONGODB_URI=mongodb+srv://USERNAME:PASSWORD@cluster0.xxxxx.mongodb.net/week9_db?retryWrites=true&w=majority

JWT_SECRET=your_access_token_secret
JWT_EXPIRE=1h

EMAIL_USER=your_email@gmail.com
EMAIL_PASS=your_app_password
EMAIL_FROM=your_email@gmail.com

APP_NAME=My Awesome App
FRONTEND_URL=http://localhost:3000

CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=your_cloud_name
CLOUDINARY_API_KEY=your_api_key
CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET=your_api_secret
```

### 3. Run

```bash
node app.js
```

Expected:

```
✅ Email server is ready to send messages
✅ MongoDB connected successfully
🚀 Server running on port 3000
```

