# 🧪 Postman Testing Flow

```
1. Register user
       ↓
2. Check inbox for welcome email
       ↓
3. Login → copy JWT token
       ↓
4. GET /api/users?page=1&limit=5      → pagination metadata
       ↓
5. GET /api/users?role=admin&search=example&sort=-createdAt&fields=name,email
       ↓
6. POST /api/users/upload-avatar (form-data → avatar)
       ↓
7. POST /api/users/upload-avatar again with different image → old auto-deleted
       ↓
8. DELETE /api/users/avatar           → removed from Cloudinary + DB
       ↓
9. POST /api/users/forgot-password    → check inbox for reset email
```

Exported Postman collection: `week-9.postman_collection.json`

---

# 🧠 Key Concepts Learned

- Pagination with skip/limit and metadata
- Max limit enforcement and out-of-range page handling
- Allowlist pattern for safe query filtering
- Regex escaping to prevent ReDoS
- Case-insensitive text search across multiple fields
- Sorting with direction prefix
- Field selection to shrink responses
- Combining pagination + filter + sort + search safely
- Nodemailer with Gmail App Password
- HTML email templates with dynamic values
- Failing gracefully when an email fails
- Multer + Cloudinary for cloud file storage
- Storing and using `publicId` to replace/delete images
- Avoiding local disk storage for uploads

---

# 🔐 Security Notes

| Feature | Handling |
|---------|----------|
| Password storage | bcrypt, 10 rounds + salt |
| Password in responses | Never returned |
| JWT secret | In `.env`, not in code |
| Token expiry | 1 hour default |
| Query injection | Allowlist of approved parameters |
| Regex injection | Special characters escaped |
| File upload | 5 MB size limit + format validation |
| Cloudinary secret | In `.env` |

